# So the rule belongs where the whole delay is visible, which is the reader, and the
# frame already carries what it needs: `ts`. That is now written into the contract's
# conventions rather than left as an assumption about clients. What the client-side
# deadline still buys is the other half, and it is why it stays: it stops the pump
# waiting behind a write nobody wants any more, which is the ordering cost this design is
# built to avoid.
